§ `s 32`

`a former employee telling a journalist about a project` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `is or was a director, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS TRUE
    `the information was obtained in the course of duties` IS TRUE
    `disclosed for the performance of duties` IS FALSE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS FALSE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

`an employee giving a rival a supplier's tender price` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `is or was a director, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS TRUE
    `the information was obtained in the course of duties` IS TRUE
    `disclosed for the performance of duties` IS FALSE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS FALSE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

`an employee answering a court order` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `is or was a director, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS TRUE
    `the information was obtained in the course of duties` IS TRUE
    `disclosed for the performance of duties` IS FALSE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS TRUE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

`an employee briefing a supplier as part of the job` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `is or was a director, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS TRUE
    `the information was obtained in the course of duties` IS TRUE
    `disclosed for the performance of duties` IS TRUE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS FALSE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

`a member of the public who found a document` MEANS Disclosure WITH
    `is or was a director, officer, employee, agent or committee member` IS FALSE
    `the information was obtained in the course of duties` IS TRUE
    `disclosed for the performance of duties` IS FALSE
    `lawfully required by a court` IS FALSE
    `required or allowed by written law` IS FALSE

#ASSERT `the disclosure is an offence under section 32` `a former employee telling a journalist about a project`
#ASSERT `the disclosure is an offence under section 32` `an employee giving a rival a supplier's tender price`
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure is an offence under section 32` `an employee answering a court order`
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure is an offence under section 32` `an employee briefing a supplier as part of the job`
#ASSERT NOT `the disclosure is an offence under section 32` `a member of the public who found a document`

